---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How The Practitioners Pod handles your data.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mono">Last updated: October 2, 2026</p>
      <p>This site is intentionally simple. Here's exactly what we collect and why.</p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> your email address, used only to tell you about new episodes.</li>
        <li><strong>Guest applications and contact forms:</strong> the details you submit, used only to respond to you and evaluate guest fit.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> our host (Netlify) keeps standard server logs, such as IP address and user agent, for security and reliability.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't sell or rent your data, and we don't use advertising trackers. Form submissions are stored by Netlify, our form processor.</p>
      <h2>Embedded players</h2>
      <p>
        Episode pages may embed YouTube (privacy-enhanced mode) or Spotify players. Those services may set their own cookies when you
        press play; their privacy policies apply.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from emails at any time, or ask us to delete anything you've submitted by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
